      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 The Society of Thoracic Surgeons. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "When identified, rib fractures in children are associated with high-energy trauma, nonaccidental trauma, or both. Traditionally, the optimal management of rib fractures in children is supportive care. In this case report, we present a 6-year-old boy who underwent surgical rib fixation for multiple displaced and comminuted rib fractures after being stepped on by a horse."
      },
